      "problem": "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $12\\,\\text{cm},$ $2\\,\\text{cm},$ and $6\\,\\text{cm},$ respectively?",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=12\\,\\text{cm},\\,w=2\\,\\text{cm},\\,h=6\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=12\\cdot 2\\cdot 6=144\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$",
